WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:03.920
WRITTEN BY HYUGA NATSU

01:32.050 --> 01:33.760
THIS STORY IS A FICTION AND ALL NAMES OF
FIGURES AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTITIOUS.

01:33.843 --> 01:34.844
MOREOVER, THE STORY HAS NO RELATION
TO REAL-LIFE INCIDENTS AND EVENTS.

01:37.430 --> 01:40.225
<i>Rumors tend to spread rapidly.</i>

01:40.850 --> 01:43.853
<i>The further and wider they spread,</i>
<i>the more they deviate from the truth.</i>

01:43.937 --> 01:46.731
<i>At times, rumors cease</i>
<i>to remain mere rumors…</i>

01:48.191 --> 01:49.818
<i>Legends and myths</i>

01:49.901 --> 01:52.487
<i>may be somewhat similar in that regard.</i>

01:55.907 --> 01:56.741
I'm leaving.

01:57.325 --> 01:58.493
Take care.

01:59.911 --> 02:02.413
<i>An overgrown peach orchard</i>
<i>to the north of the rear palace.</i>

02:02.997 --> 02:05.917
<i>Nearby is an old shrine-like building.</i>

02:06.000 --> 02:07.293
<i>And a pond.</i>

02:08.628 --> 02:09.838
<i>It is said that in the past,</i>

02:09.921 --> 02:12.298
<i>another people once lived in this area,</i>

02:12.382 --> 02:14.467
<i>and the remaining structures, outer walls,</i>

02:14.551 --> 02:17.929
<i>and underground waterways</i>
<i>are still in use today.</i>

02:19.556 --> 02:21.266
-Whoa.
-Guess who?

02:22.100 --> 02:22.976
Shisui.

02:24.018 --> 02:26.354
Correct! Was it my voice
that gave it away?

02:27.105 --> 02:28.731
<i>This friendliness…</i>

02:28.815 --> 02:30.942
<i>As expected of Xiaolan’s chatting buddy.</i>

02:32.193 --> 02:33.862
Maomao, what are you doing here?

02:33.945 --> 02:36.614
What about you, Shisui? Why are you here?

02:36.698 --> 02:39.659
Me? I just have a little errand to run.

02:42.036 --> 02:43.621
-Snacking?
-No, but…

02:43.705 --> 02:45.331
Look at this!

02:50.920 --> 02:52.839
Isn't it cute?

02:52.922 --> 02:55.550
Normally, this would be
considered harassment,

02:55.633 --> 02:57.093
so it’s better not to do it.

02:57.176 --> 03:00.889
Eh? Why? It’s so cute!

03:02.432 --> 03:04.559
This place really is amazing, isn’t it?

03:04.642 --> 03:07.103
There are many insects here
that I've only seen in picture books.

03:07.186 --> 03:09.355
This is the first time
I've seen this bug too!

03:09.939 --> 03:11.566
Huh, is that so?

03:12.442 --> 03:14.736
<i>This land has been trading</i>
<i>for a long time.</i>

03:14.819 --> 03:16.863
<i>This bug probably came</i>
<i>mixed in with goods from abroad</i>

03:16.946 --> 03:18.573
<i>and it successfully reproduced.</i>

03:19.365 --> 03:22.327
-Will this turn into a butterfly?
-Nope, they're moths.

03:22.410 --> 03:24.662
Since they're nocturnal,
they're not flying right now,

03:24.746 --> 03:26.080
but they are beautiful moths!

03:28.750 --> 03:31.461
<i>I wonder if they were around</i>
<i>when the old lady danced?</i>

03:32.837 --> 03:35.048
Maomao, you should come
see it at night too.

03:35.131 --> 03:37.467
It glimmers softly under the moonlight…

03:37.550 --> 03:40.553
It feels like you’ve
wandered into paradise.

03:40.637 --> 03:42.847
That’s a bit of an exaggeration…

03:44.140 --> 03:46.434
<i>Glimmering in the moonlight…</i>

03:47.018 --> 03:49.771
Do these moths mate
right after they hatch?

03:49.854 --> 03:53.775
Probably. Once they become adults,
they can’t eat food,

03:53.858 --> 03:55.818
so they die pretty quickly, I heard.

03:55.902 --> 03:59.239
Hey, can you tell the difference between
male and female moths?

03:59.322 --> 04:01.157
I think I can, roughly…

04:01.241 --> 04:02.784
Shisui!

04:02.867 --> 04:04.661
I need your help with something.

04:07.830 --> 04:10.250
<i>This might… just work!</i>

04:11.417 --> 04:12.835
Is it something bad?

04:46.661 --> 04:48.079
<i>A few days later,</i>

04:48.162 --> 04:50.665
<i>a banquet was held to welcome the envoys.</i>

04:51.416 --> 04:54.419
<i>It took place in the northern garden</i>
<i>where the "Moon Spirit"</i>

04:54.502 --> 04:55.545
<i>appeared 50 years ago.</i>

04:57.088 --> 04:59.632
<i>Normally, men are forbidden in the palace,</i>

04:59.716 --> 05:02.844
<i>but as a special exception,</i>
<i>male officials were granted entry.</i>

05:02.927 --> 05:05.263
<i>Even senior-ranking consorts</i>
<i>participated in the event.</i>

05:06.347 --> 05:09.267
<i>Attendees enjoyed the banquet</i>
<i>from inside their carriages.</i>

05:10.643 --> 05:12.979
<i>This was also a gesture</i>
<i>to avoid treating the foreign envoys</i>

05:13.062 --> 05:14.981
<i>as mere spectacles…</i>

05:17.066 --> 05:19.485
Blue eyes and golden hair…

05:19.569 --> 05:21.029
Such beauties.

05:21.112 --> 05:23.114
We can't deceive them with bad actors.

05:24.198 --> 05:26.492
<i>Moreover, raising their curtain</i>
<i>all the way up</i>

05:26.576 --> 05:28.202
<i>to allow the Emperor to see their faces</i>

05:28.286 --> 05:30.538
<i>shows just how much confidence they have.</i>

05:31.748 --> 05:34.917
<i>Above all, while the demure beauty</i>
<i>sitting in the back is striking,</i>

05:35.001 --> 05:36.169
<i>the ones in the front</i>

05:36.252 --> 05:39.756
<i>are full of confidence, knowing that</i>
<i>they are more beautiful than anyone else.</i>

05:40.339 --> 05:42.925
<i>There’s no doubt that</i>
<i>these two foreign beauties</i>

05:43.009 --> 05:46.262
<i>are stunning enough to rival</i>
<i>the senior-ranking consorts.</i>

05:56.314 --> 05:59.150
<i>The performances and music</i>
<i>are flashier than usual.</i>

05:59.233 --> 06:01.444
<i>It must be tailored to suit the envoys.</i>

06:01.527 --> 06:02.695
<i>But…</i>

06:02.779 --> 06:05.156
<i>they look rather bored themselves.</i>

06:05.239 --> 06:07.450
<i>Are they trying to say it’s disappointing?</i>

06:08.284 --> 06:10.203
Even so, they really do look alike…

06:11.120 --> 06:14.749
<i>I heard they’re cousins who share the same</i>
<i>grandfather, but they look like twins.</i>

06:15.249 --> 06:17.418
<i>If it’s those two, the "mirror story"</i>

06:17.502 --> 06:19.629
<i>that Lord Gaoshun mentioned</i>
<i>might actually be possible.</i>

06:32.975 --> 06:36.270
Good day. Even though this is
such a rare banquet,

06:36.354 --> 06:38.106
it’s such a shame
we’re seated so far apart.

06:39.107 --> 06:41.943
I would much prefer
to talk a little closer.

06:43.069 --> 06:46.155
I heard the Emperor’s younger brother
is absent today.

06:46.739 --> 06:48.991
I was really hoping to meet him.

06:51.577 --> 06:54.831
<i>Ugh, scary. Truly scary…</i>

06:55.832 --> 06:57.875
<i>The true purpose of the special envoys</i>

06:57.959 --> 06:59.293
<i>is to gain the favor of</i>

06:59.919 --> 07:01.587
<i>the Emperor and his brother,</i>

07:01.671 --> 07:04.173
<i>securing marriage ties with them.</i>

07:04.257 --> 07:06.801
<i>Probably for political reasons.</i>

07:06.884 --> 07:08.719
If it pleases you…

07:08.803 --> 07:09.762
Ayla,

07:10.930 --> 07:14.267
you should head back soon.
It's a rare performance,

07:14.767 --> 07:16.477
and you ought to enjoy it properly.

07:18.980 --> 07:20.648
My apologies.

07:28.197 --> 07:29.115
Hongniang!

07:29.198 --> 07:31.242
<i>Somehow they managed.</i>

07:31.325 --> 07:32.368
<i>I was so nervous.</i>

07:33.744 --> 07:35.371
<i>The two beauties may not be interested</i>

07:35.455 --> 07:37.665
<i>in the most beautiful woman</i>

07:37.748 --> 07:39.375
<i>that their grandfather saw.</i>

07:40.334 --> 07:42.920
<i>"There's no one more beautiful</i>
<i>in the world than ourselves."</i>

07:43.004 --> 07:44.964
<i>That's how they take pride in themselves.</i>

07:45.756 --> 07:48.885
<i>At this rate, the reason they gave</i>
<i>mirrors to the four consorts</i>

07:48.968 --> 07:51.429
<i>might have been a form of provocation.</i>

07:52.180 --> 07:54.307
<i>Well, it’s fine. My job is</i>

07:54.390 --> 07:56.726
<i>to show those two the Moon Spirit.</i>

08:01.898 --> 08:04.901
It seems like the banquet is about to end.
How's it going?

08:05.735 --> 08:08.946
I've done everything… I could.

08:11.073 --> 08:14.243
<i>Well, that’s the kind of reaction</i>
<i>I’d expect.</i>

08:16.579 --> 08:18.623
Shall we go?

08:25.630 --> 08:27.798
The music seemed to have been
made more extravagant

08:27.882 --> 08:29.800
to suit us,

08:29.884 --> 08:32.970
but the dance wasn’t anything special,
was it, Aylin?

08:34.096 --> 08:37.350
Even the so-called four consorts
remained hidden behind the screens.

08:37.433 --> 08:40.770
Regarding the Moon Spirit our grandfather
saw, how impressive could it really be?

08:40.853 --> 08:44.106
Ayla, this isn’t the place
to talk about that.

08:44.982 --> 08:46.692
We can talk in my room afterwards.

08:49.278 --> 08:53.157
We might hear from the Emperor
himself any moment now.

09:10.716 --> 09:11.884
<i>This guy!</i>

09:34.991 --> 09:35.825
<i>Fifty years ago,</i>

09:36.909 --> 09:39.662
<i>the scene the envoy's grandfather saw</i>

09:39.745 --> 09:41.372
<i>could have been something like this.</i>

10:04.770 --> 10:06.147
Diana.

10:09.358 --> 10:11.235
<i>I wasn’t confident</i>
<i>about the pronunciation,</i>

10:11.319 --> 10:12.987
<i>but it seems to have gotten across.</i>

10:16.532 --> 10:18.242
<i>The name of the Moon Goddess</i>

10:18.326 --> 10:20.119
<i>from the West.</i>

10:22.580 --> 10:23.706
It seems to have gone well.

10:23.789 --> 10:27.335
Yes, I think it turned out as I expected.

10:28.002 --> 10:29.837
<i>If you remove the black cloth in the dark,</i>

10:29.920 --> 10:32.548
it seems as though he suddenly appears.

10:33.049 --> 10:35.551
Above all, the key is those moths.

10:36.218 --> 10:38.054
<i>In the painting of the old lady,</i>

10:38.137 --> 10:40.264
<i>the light that shines</i>

10:40.348 --> 10:41.641
<i>is of an adult moth.</i>

10:42.350 --> 10:44.393
The old lady said that
they were bothering her.

10:44.477 --> 10:45.895
<i>On the day of the event,</i>

10:45.978 --> 10:48.272
<i>there were people who played</i>
<i>a prank on my outfit.</i>

10:48.356 --> 10:51.275
<i>They rubbed insect corpses onto it.</i>

10:52.443 --> 10:54.528
<i>Among insects, some emit a scent</i>

10:54.612 --> 10:56.030
<i>to attract the opposite sex.</i>

10:56.906 --> 10:58.824
<i>The males, attracted to the smell,</i>

10:58.908 --> 11:00.660
<i>gathered around the old lady.</i>

11:00.743 --> 11:04.497
<i>They looked like moon spirits</i>
<i>dancing in the light.</i>

11:04.997 --> 11:06.582
<i>What a coincidence…</i>

11:07.083 --> 11:11.045
<i>I need to thank Shisui</i>
<i>and Xiaolan for their help.</i>

11:12.713 --> 11:16.801
<i>But it was difficult to show</i>
<i>that view only to the envoys.</i>

11:17.843 --> 11:21.055
<i>I had already instructed the coachman</i>
<i>not to look this way.</i>

11:21.555 --> 11:23.808
<i>Lord Gaoshun and his men</i>
<i>were on standby nearby,</i>

11:23.891 --> 11:26.852
<i>ready to jump into action</i>
<i>if anything was to happen.</i>

11:27.645 --> 11:30.064
<i>That is not something</i>
<i>to be shown to everyone.</i>

11:31.065 --> 11:32.149
<i>A beauty…</i>

11:32.233 --> 11:35.403
<i>so captivating that</i>
<i>he could topple a kingdom.</i>

11:36.237 --> 11:37.071
<i>Hey!</i>

11:38.030 --> 11:40.074
I did what you said
and you just leave me stranded?

11:41.534 --> 11:44.286
Thank you, Lord Jinshi.

11:44.370 --> 11:47.540
For swimming across the pond
with that heavy outfit on.

11:48.332 --> 11:50.209
So did it go well?

11:50.292 --> 11:53.129
Yes, I believe I fulfilled

11:53.212 --> 11:55.589
the envoy's request to the utmost.

11:56.424 --> 11:59.093
Well, I did my job!

11:59.176 --> 12:00.594
My hair's still wet!

12:09.061 --> 12:11.188
<i>Why don't you do it yourself?</i>

12:20.531 --> 12:22.867
Then, fine.

12:32.543 --> 12:33.669
Oh, Maomao.

12:34.587 --> 12:37.047
I'm going to the new school!

12:38.340 --> 12:40.843
<i>Oh, it opened without any issues.</i>

12:40.926 --> 12:43.512
I'm going to be a first-year student!

12:43.596 --> 12:45.389
I'm off then.

12:45.473 --> 12:46.807
Do your best.

12:58.027 --> 12:59.570
<i>I'm so bored.</i>

13:00.070 --> 13:03.824
<i>There isn't much work to do</i>
<i>back at the Jade Pavilion either…</i>

13:04.408 --> 13:05.868
<i>The quack doctor's place is…</i>

13:05.951 --> 13:09.330
<i>probably swamped</i>
<i>with the perfume incident.</i>

13:10.372 --> 13:12.082
<i>That perfume incident</i>

13:12.166 --> 13:14.251
<i>isn't completely over.</i>

13:15.169 --> 13:17.213
<i>Even if each individual amount is small,</i>

13:17.296 --> 13:19.256
<i>it can become a poison</i>
<i>depending on the combination.</i>

13:20.049 --> 13:23.761
<i>Who in the world would arrange</i>
<i>for such a thing to be brought in?</i>

13:24.803 --> 13:26.180
I'm investigating, but

13:26.263 --> 13:29.266
each Pavilion purchased
a large amount of perfume.

13:30.017 --> 13:32.228
The attendants of
the Jade Pavilion did too.

13:32.311 --> 13:34.522
I had anything poisonous disposed of, but…

13:35.064 --> 13:37.900
For example, is there
any possibility that the envoys

13:37.983 --> 13:39.151
could have arranged this?

13:39.235 --> 13:42.154
I wonder. Perhaps their aim was to

13:42.238 --> 13:46.408
infiltrate the ranks of the consorts.

13:46.492 --> 13:48.077
But their pride must be so shattered,

13:48.160 --> 13:50.454
it's not worth their time.

13:57.002 --> 13:59.547
<i>There are four high-ranking consorts</i>
<i>in the palace.</i>

14:00.381 --> 14:01.966
<i>Considering their families' power,</i>

14:02.716 --> 14:05.594
<i>the most important one</i>
<i>would be Consort Loulan.</i>

14:06.512 --> 14:08.305
<i>Her father, Shishou,</i>

14:08.389 --> 14:11.392
<i>was a favored minister who was</i>
<i>highly-regarded by the previous emperor.</i>

14:11.976 --> 14:14.562
<i>The current emperor visits him regularly,</i>

14:15.229 --> 14:17.690
<i>but his enthusiasm doesn't seem very high.</i>

14:18.649 --> 14:21.777
<i>The next highest-ranking consort</i>
<i>is Consort Lihua,</i>

14:21.861 --> 14:24.613
<i>but due to being</i>
<i>a relative of the emperor,</i>

14:24.697 --> 14:26.991
<i>she isn't the ambitious type.</i>

14:27.575 --> 14:30.035
<i>She fell ill after losing</i>
<i>her crown prince,</i>

14:30.119 --> 14:33.080
<i>but she has regained the emperor's favor.</i>

14:34.540 --> 14:35.666
<i>On the other hand,</i>

14:35.749 --> 14:38.919
<i>the family of Consort Lishu who</i>
<i>has risen in rank in recent generations,</i>

14:39.003 --> 14:42.798
<i>is so ambitious, having offered their</i>
<i>young daughter to the previous emperor.</i>

14:43.299 --> 14:47.261
<i>Unfortunately, the emperor</i>
<i>prefers fuller-bodied women,</i>

14:47.887 --> 14:49.638
<i>and even after Consort Ah-Duo left,</i>

14:49.722 --> 14:51.640
<i>she hasn't become his consort.</i>

14:52.725 --> 14:56.353
<i>On the other hand, the emperor favors</i>
<i>Consort Gyokuyou the most.</i>

14:56.979 --> 14:58.731
<i>In addition to having their daughter,</i>
<i>Princess Lingli,</i>

14:58.814 --> 15:01.233
<i>she is pregnant</i>
<i>with the emperor's child again.</i>

15:02.109 --> 15:04.111
<i>Her homeland, the western country,</i>

15:04.194 --> 15:06.614
<i>seems to be prosperous from trade,</i>

15:06.697 --> 15:08.490
<i>but the land is barren</i>

15:08.574 --> 15:10.784
<i>and it's not exactly prosperous.</i>

15:11.577 --> 15:13.537
<i>Consort Gyokuyou has twice</i>
<i>been the victim of</i>

15:13.621 --> 15:15.539
<i>an attempted assassination</i>
<i>by poison in the past.</i>

15:17.082 --> 15:19.752
<i>The incident at the garden party</i>
<i>last year was</i>

15:19.835 --> 15:21.754
<i>carried out by</i>
<i>the head attendant of Consort Ah-Duo,</i>

15:21.837 --> 15:24.673
<i>who acted on her own</i>
<i>to target Consort Lishu.</i>

15:25.758 --> 15:28.218
<i>But the reason wasn't for power,</i>

15:28.302 --> 15:31.347
<i>it was a very human motive.</i>

15:32.097 --> 15:33.766
<i>But before that,</i>

15:33.849 --> 15:37.519
<i>who poisoned Consort Gyokuyou when</i>
<i>she was pregnant with Princess Lingli?</i>

15:37.603 --> 15:39.063
<i>Who could it have been?</i>

15:39.813 --> 15:42.232
<i>If Lady Hongniang is right,</i>

15:42.316 --> 15:46.070
<i>the culprit is the mid-ranking consort</i>
<i>who died in the recent mushroom incident.</i>

15:46.654 --> 15:48.238
<i>However, how did the mid-ranking consort</i>

15:48.322 --> 15:51.450
<i>acquire knowledge of poison?</i>

15:52.534 --> 15:53.744
<i>Suirei.</i>

15:54.912 --> 15:57.081
<i>Her whereabouts are still unknown.</i>

15:58.207 --> 16:00.834
<i>Why…? For what reason…?</i>

16:00.918 --> 16:03.545
What was her goal
in targeting Lord Jinshi?

16:05.089 --> 16:09.176
It's useless for
a mere poison tester to think about this?

16:09.843 --> 16:12.179
I think I'll do something
to clear my head.

16:16.350 --> 16:18.394
<i>Cherry season is almost over…</i>

16:20.396 --> 16:22.606
<i>Those are the attendants</i>
<i>from the Crystal Pavilion.</i>

16:23.399 --> 16:24.566
Oh my!

16:27.903 --> 16:30.531
<i>They're making a big fuss over nothing.</i>

16:33.575 --> 16:35.411
<i>She's the only attendant</i>

16:35.494 --> 16:37.788
<i>in the Crystal Pavilion</i>
<i>who doesn't wear any perfume.</i>

16:42.292 --> 16:46.005
<i>I thought it was unusual</i>
<i>in the fashion-conscious Crystal Palace,</i>

16:46.672 --> 16:48.298
<i>but maybe there's at least one person…</i>

16:54.805 --> 16:57.558
I'm feeling a bit under the weather.

16:57.641 --> 16:59.476
Don't get sick.

16:59.560 --> 17:02.646
What if you pass it on to
Lady Gyokuyou and the others?

17:02.730 --> 17:04.565
I was being careful…

17:06.608 --> 17:09.111
You have a slight fever.

17:09.194 --> 17:11.238
Should I make you
some herbal medicine for a cold?

17:11.321 --> 17:13.907
Then, after you make the medicine,

17:13.991 --> 17:16.785
could you take her to the clinic?

17:16.869 --> 17:18.787
The clinic?

17:19.413 --> 17:21.331
It's different from the medical office.

17:21.415 --> 17:23.584
Anyway, Ailan knows about it.

17:23.667 --> 17:26.545
-So, please take her there.
-Understood.

17:31.175 --> 17:34.344
<i>I had no idea there was a place</i>
<i>like this in the north of the palace.</i>

17:35.345 --> 17:37.306
<i>Having a laundry nearby is</i>

17:37.389 --> 17:40.517
<i>quite practical for frequent washing</i>
<i>of clothes and bedding.</i>

17:41.101 --> 17:43.353
-Excuse me, I think I've caught a cold.
-Huh?

17:44.646 --> 17:46.815
<i>It's rare to see</i>
<i>a middle-aged palace woman.</i>

17:48.525 --> 17:50.944
You have a slight fever.
Stick out your tongue.

17:53.489 --> 17:55.741
It doesn't seem too bad.

17:56.366 --> 17:59.703
You'll be fine as long as you don't
overexert yourself for a few days.

17:59.787 --> 18:00.829
What do you want to do?

18:00.913 --> 18:03.874
I can't infect the consorts,

18:03.957 --> 18:06.376
so could I please
stay the night here just to be safe?

18:07.211 --> 18:08.670
Come with me.

18:08.754 --> 18:11.423
<i>She's much more experienced</i>
<i>than that quack doctor,</i>

18:11.507 --> 18:13.634
<i>and she's very good at diagnosis.</i>

18:16.637 --> 18:19.556
I can't stand this smell.

18:19.640 --> 18:21.600
It smells like alcohol.

18:21.683 --> 18:23.519
It's a sign of cleanliness.

18:24.561 --> 18:27.022
There are many windows,
so it's well-ventilated.

18:27.106 --> 18:30.442
Despite its simplicity, it's very clean.

18:30.526 --> 18:32.694
I think it's the perfect place
for recuperation.

18:34.696 --> 18:36.365
Please use this room.

18:36.448 --> 18:38.283
Thank you.

18:38.367 --> 18:41.370
Maomao, tell them I'll be back tomorrow.

18:41.453 --> 18:42.287
Understood.

18:47.417 --> 18:49.253
<i>Sick attendants</i>

18:49.336 --> 18:52.131
<i>are isolated like this, huh?</i>

18:52.214 --> 18:54.842
You go back to work.

18:54.925 --> 18:58.053
Don't think you can slack off
just because you're accompanying her.

18:58.137 --> 18:59.429
What is it?

18:59.513 --> 19:02.850
Or are you going to fold
all the laundry here?

19:03.892 --> 19:06.061
Excuse me!

19:07.563 --> 19:10.566
<i>I knew I couldn't beat the older lady…</i>

19:10.649 --> 19:12.568
<i>Nevertheless,</i>

19:12.651 --> 19:15.237
<i>there are only older palace women here.</i>

19:15.320 --> 19:17.197
In the rear palace, when you get older,

19:17.281 --> 19:19.449
you're almost forced to be replaced,

19:20.367 --> 19:23.078
but in the clinic, experience
and knowledge are necessary,

19:23.162 --> 19:25.205
so they can probably stay longer…

19:27.416 --> 19:31.378
Don't mumble to yourself
as you walk. You'll trip.

19:31.461 --> 19:33.547
Was I saying something?

19:35.132 --> 19:37.551
Is there something you need?

19:38.260 --> 19:40.387
No, I don't need anything, but

19:41.054 --> 19:43.515
is it wrong to talk to someone
I happen to meet?

19:47.186 --> 19:50.063
-Where were you at?
-The clinic.

19:50.147 --> 19:52.399
I didn't know there was a place like that.

19:52.482 --> 19:53.901
When you first entered the palace,

19:53.984 --> 19:57.821
you were supposed to be shown everything,
but I guess it was overlooked.

19:58.405 --> 20:01.241
I probably wasn't listening at the time

20:01.325 --> 20:03.160
because I had been sold and was so upset.

20:05.329 --> 20:09.833
<i>Every time I talk about this,</i>
<i>I get kind of depressed.</i>

20:11.084 --> 20:14.296
I was surprised by
how well-equipped it was.

20:14.379 --> 20:17.591
Actually, shouldn't that place be
the medical office?

20:18.508 --> 20:20.802
If that were possible, it would be great.

20:20.886 --> 20:22.721
What do you mean?

20:22.804 --> 20:24.973
Because only men can be medical officers.

20:26.016 --> 20:28.143
<i>Minor injuries are one thing, but</i>

20:28.227 --> 20:30.938
<i>only medical officers can</i>
<i>handle serious injuries.</i>

20:31.521 --> 20:34.942
<i>And of course, only medical officers</i>
<i>can prepare medicine.</i>

20:35.734 --> 20:38.403
<i>That's why there was</i>
<i>no smell of medicine in the clinic.</i>

20:38.487 --> 20:39.947
<i>I see.</i>

20:40.781 --> 20:42.491
What will happen to me?

20:43.784 --> 20:45.827
Turn a blind eye to it.

20:46.411 --> 20:50.332
<i>There seems to be</i>
<i>some complicated circumstances involved.</i>

20:50.415 --> 20:52.417
For the future,

20:52.501 --> 20:55.837
we should find a different way
to recruit medical officers.

20:57.005 --> 20:59.007
So that one can become one
without being a eunuch.

21:00.634 --> 21:02.010
<i>Eunuchs…</i>

21:03.220 --> 21:05.389
<i>After the current emperor took the throne,</i>

21:05.472 --> 21:08.684
<i>the surgery to become a eunuch</i>
<i>was banned. So in the future,</i>

21:09.685 --> 21:12.271
<i>it's clear that there will be</i>
<i>a shortage of manpower.</i>

21:12.854 --> 21:15.148
<i>Considering Lord Jinshi's age,</i>

21:15.232 --> 21:18.777
<i>he probably had the surgery</i>
<i>just before it was banned.</i>

21:19.361 --> 21:22.656
It's a pity. If he had
waited a few more years…

21:24.241 --> 21:25.075
What?

21:25.701 --> 21:27.327
<i>Oops, I said it out loud.</i>

21:29.329 --> 21:31.373
Lord Jinshi, you still have other work.

21:32.416 --> 21:33.625
Understood.

21:35.961 --> 21:36.878
And, apothecary,

21:38.213 --> 21:41.883
make sure no one else knows
that you're preparing medicine.

21:41.967 --> 21:43.552
Understood.

21:48.557 --> 21:51.393
<i>If I made a growth potion,</i>
<i>would I make a profit?</i>

21:56.440 --> 21:58.191
That's medicine, isn't it?

21:59.359 --> 22:01.528
The maid I saw earlier
smelled of medicine.

22:03.822 --> 22:05.073
That maid…

22:05.866 --> 22:08.452
She's secretly making medicine, isn't she?

23:46.007 --> 23:49.052
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

23:56.643 --> 24:00.355
<i>The next episode is</i>
<i>"Once Again, Crystal Pavilion."</i>
